CommitDate: Wed Nov 4 17:00:47 2026 +0100

    fix(piv): align extraction errors and validate recovery witnesses
    
    Restore source-correct V1 symbols in migration examples and import Core cryptography in the V2 key-generation example. Report unknown parsed metadata algorithms as NotSupportedException from both extractors while retaining recognized-family errors.
    
    Reject stale derived authentication at witness submission, independently validate the derived witness, and simulate protected restoration success or changed-key rejection. Retain first-stage cancellation/status coverage and assert original authentication payload/response buffers are cleared before disposal without production hooks.
    
    Verify known RSA/EC metadata extraction against generated public keys on hardware. Focused regressions: 19 passed; PIV units: 264 passed; final hardware subset: 18 passed; final reset: 1 passed. Full clean solution build has zero warnings/errors; scoped formatting and complexity pass.

